"] "\n" [:option {:value "311071"} "Sabre, Individual, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "311386"} "Sabre, Team, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "311000"} "Foil, Individual, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "311412"} "Foil, Team, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "311142"} "Épée, Individual, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "311438"} "Épée, Team, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "311322"} "Sabre, Individual, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "9009289"} "1889"] "\n" [:option {:value "9009290"} "1889"] "\n" [:option {:value "72000"} "1896"] "\n" [:option {:value "72031"} "1900"] "\n" [:option {:value "72237"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "72277"} "1906"] "\n" [:option {:value "73551"} "1912"] "\n" [:option {:value "73962"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "74111"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "77141"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "80451"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "81894"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "85856"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "86512"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "86748"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "86895"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "90541"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "93474"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "96653"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "100009"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "103487"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "105440"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "108488"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "112098"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "114619"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "115844"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "116887"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "259119"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "357450"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016400"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2010900"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/278"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Foil, Individual, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "31 July 2012"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/861"} "ExCeL, Newham, London"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/311213"} "38 from 20 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Italy and Germany were expected to do well in the foil. Italian " [:a {:href "/athletes/106027"} "Andrea Cassarà"] " had won the 2011 world title, defeating compatriot " [:a {:href "/athletes/123947"} "Valerio Aspromonte"] " in the final in Catania. Cassarà was also ranked first in the FIE rankings, although Aspromonte was seeded first in the Olympic tournament. Third Italian on the squad was " [:a {:href "/athletes/123949"} "Andrea Baldini"] ". He had missed the 2008 Games, after it was reported he had failed a drug test. He was cleared of the accusations several months later, immediately earning the World and European titles of 2009. Germany had entered defending champion, " [:a {:href "/athletes/118195"} "Benjamin Kleibrink"] ", and the four-time World Champion, " [:a {:href "/athletes/106034"} "Peter Joppich"] ". Earlier in the 2012 season, " [:a {:href "/athletes/118198"} "Lei Sheng"] " had earned the Asian title, while European gold was claimed by " [:a {:href "/athletes/120337"} "Aleksey Cheremisinov"] ", two months before the Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The first casualties fell in the round of 32, where Kleibrink was served revenge by " [:a {:href "/athletes/106046"} "Yuki Ota"] ", who had lost the 2008 Olympic final to him. Joppich suffered defeat at the hands of " [:a {:href "/athletes/123357"} "Alaaeldin Abouelkassem"] ", the 2010 Junior World Champion. Abouelkassem, son of an Egyptian father and Algerian mother, had suffered his father’s death just a few months before the Olympics, but this did not stop him from upsetting also Cassarà in the quarter-finals. Lei Sheng, a three-time World Championship medallist, took care of the other two Italians, outscoring Aspromonte in the quarter-finals, and Baldini in the semis. The Chinese and the Egyptian met in the final, where Lei took a 8-5 lead in the first period. Abouelkassem recovered to lead by two points at 13-11, but then received four touches in a row to give the title to Lei. With the bronze taken by " [:a {:href "/athletes/106036"} "Choi Byeong-Cheol"] " of South Korea, the entire podium was taken by non-European fencers. This had not happened since 1904, when only Cuban and American foil fencers competed."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Seed"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "8"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/118198"} "Lei Sheng"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "7"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/123357"} "Alaaeldin Abouelkassem"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/EGY"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/EGY.png"}] "EGY"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "6"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/106036"} "Choi Byeong-Cheol"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KOR.png"}] "KOR"]] [:t